Start the bot, then test each feature from Telegram. Here's the full test checklist:

1. Start the bot

cd ~/elderbot && bun run dev

2. Send these commands in Telegram:

/help          → should show all commands
/status        → uptime, environment, owner ID configured
/security      → channel auth status
/today         → today's daily note summary
/note hello world   → saves a note, check /today after
/recall elderbot    → searches memory, should find project files
/memory        → shows indexed file count (should be 10+ files)
/crons         → shows 4 jobs: heartbeat, briefing, consolidation, security-review
/sessions      → should say "No active sessions"
/session start test-project   → creates a session
/sessions      → should now show the test session
/briefing      → sends you the morning briefing right now
/heartbeat     → runs a heartbeat check
/consolidate   → runs nightly consolidation manually
/lesson always test before pushing   → logs to tacit knowledge

3. Check the audit log (in a second terminal):

tail -f ~/elderbot/logs/security.log

You should see every command logged with timestamps.
